### PART D — WHICH TOOL IS BETTER FOR WHICH VULNERABILITY?

| Vulnerability/research area | Ettercap       | Bettercap |
| --------------------------- | -------------- | --------- |
| ARP spoofing resistance     | Strong         | Strong    |
| Network reconnaissance      | Yes            | Strong    |
| DNS weaknesses              | Yes            | Yes       |
| Cleartext traffic           | Yes            | Yes       |
| TLS configuration           | Limited        | Limited   |
| Wi-Fi security              | Limited        | Stronger  |
| Bluetooth LE                | No major focus | Yes       |
| HTTP traffic analysis       | Yes            | Yes       |
| API authorization           | No             | No        |
| SQL injection               | No             | No        |
| Insecure deserialization    | No             | No        |
| RCE                         | No             | No        |
| IDOR                        | No             | No        |
| Race conditions             | No             | No        |

Do not confuse network observation with vulnerability discovery. For example, seeing an HTTP request does not prove that the application has an exploitable vulnerability.

